  "tips": {
    "transportation": "Get a T-money card (rechargeable transit card) at convenience stores. Use subway for everything - cheap and efficient. Airport bus to Myeongdong: ~₩10,000.",
    "language": "English widely spoken in tourist areas. Learn basic: Annyeonghaseyo (hello), Gamsahamnida (thank you), Eodi isseoyo (where is it), Sillyehamnida (excuse me).",
    "bestTime": "October is PERFECT - fall foliage, mild weather (60-70°F), fewer crowds than summer, great food season with ginseng chicken soup.",
    "crowds": "Popular spots busy 11 AM - 4 PM. Go early morning (9 AM) or evening. Avoid lunch hours at famous restaurants.",
    "currency": "Korean Won (₩). ATMs everywhere. Most places accept cards, but small old places want cash. 1 USD ≈ 1,200 KRW.",
    "safety": "Seoul is very safe. Petty theft rare but watch bags in crowded markets. Public transit is the safest, fastest way to explore."
  }
